// go.work pins the multi-module workspace so language servers (gopls)
// resolve every package in this tree without per-file "not in workspace
// module" diagnostics. For a single-module project the workspace
// contains just `.`; tools/ or sub-modules can be added later by
// hand-editing this file.
//
// Issue #457 origin: bantubangun-shape consumer projects without a
// go.work emitted a "not in workspace module" diagnostic for every
// open file in the IDE — noise that drowned real diagnostics. Hexago
// scaffolds this file at init so the IDE works on the first checkout.
//
// The `go` directive must be ≥ the highest `go` directive of any
// included module, and Go compares the FULL semver (major.minor.patch).
// Floor is 1.26.0: the hexago module itself declares go 1.26.0, and a
// local `replace` of hexago (the recommended dev setup) advances go.mod
// to that version on `go mod tidy` — same mechanism as goose/v3 v3.27.1
// pushing the old 1.25.7 floor (issue #545). If go.work lags the floor,
// `go build ./...` fails with "module . listed in go.work file requires
// go >= 1.26.0, but go.work lists go <older>".
go 1.26.0

use (
	.
)
